 with the cost of public works in the regions; railroads crisscrossed the country by the 1880s, electrical and telephone utilities by the 1890s, and vast bonds were issued to finance new state and municipal buildings, schools, and trams.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 875, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 797})
